    START(["<b>Calvin cycle overview</b><br/>• ⚠ Converts carbon dioxide and hydrogen-carrier compounds into glucose<br/>• ⚠ Present in all photosynthetic eukaryotes and also many photosynthetic bacteria<br/>• ⚠ In plants occurs in stroma outside thylakoid membranes"]):::safetyNode
    D2{"<b>1. Light for cycle</b><br/>• Cycle happens when light is available independent of kind of photosynthesis<br/>• Cycle does not occur in dark or during nighttime"}:::decisionNode
    C1["<b>RuBisCO carboxylation</b><br/>• ⚠ Catalyses carboxylation of RuBP a 5-carbon compound by carbon dioxide in two-step reaction<br/>• ⚠ Product of first step is enediol-enzyme complex that can capture CO2 or O2"]:::safetyNode
    D1{"<b>2. Capture by enediol complex</b><br/>• CO2 captured in second step produces unstable six-carbon compound that splits into 2 molecules of 3-phosphoglycerate<br/>• RuBisCO reacts competitively with O2 instead of CO2 in photorespiration"}:::decisionNode
    R1["<b>Phosphorylation and reduction</b><br/>• Phosphoglycerate kinase catalyses phosphorylation of 3-PGA by ATP<br/>• Glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate dehydrogenase catalyses reduction of 1,3BPGA by NADPH"]:::targetDx
    G1["<b>RuBP regeneration start</b><br/>• Five G3P molecules produce three RuBP molecules using up three molecules of ATP<br/>• Triose phosphate isomerase converts one G3P reversibly into DHAP also a 3-carbon molecule"]:::targetDx
    G2["<b>Pentose conversion to RuBP</b><br/>• R5P is converted into RuP by phosphopentose isomerase<br/>• Xu5P is converted into RuP by phosphopentose epimerase<br/>• Phosphoribulokinase phosphorylates RuP into RuBP completing the Calvin cycle"]:::targetDx
    O1["<b>Net gain and use</b><br/>• Of six G3P produced five are used to make three RuBP totaling 15 carbons with only one G3P available for conversion to hexose<br/>• Surplus G3P can be used to form starch sucrose and cellulose depending on plant needs"]:::dispoNode
    P1["<b>Photorespiration branch</b><br/>• Photorespiration turns RuBP into 3-PGA and 2-phosphoglycolate a 2-carbon molecule<br/>• Serine can be converted back to 3-phosphoglycerate"]:::altDx
    NDARK["<b>Dark reserve use</b><br/>• In dark plants release sucrose into phloem from starch reserves to provide energy"]:::altDx
    TAKE["<b>Takeaway:</b> Calvin cycle fixes carbon dioxide into triose phosphates with ATP and NADPH from light reactions."]:::dispoNode
